# Daily Driver Workspace

This directory is a [daily-driver](https://github.com/skoonin/daily-driver) workspace. It holds your background, your task tracker, {% if "job_search" in plugins %}your job search data, {% endif %}and the files that set up your chats with Claude.

## Chat with Claude

Most of the time, you start a chat with Claude. Type one of these commands in the Terminal app, inside this folder. Claude adds and updates your tasks and writes your plans and notes.

```
daily-driver day-start        # start a chat with Claude to plan your day
daily-driver check-in         # midday chat: tell Claude what is done or stuck
daily-driver day-end          # end-of-day chat: review the day and save notes
daily-driver resume           # reopen your most recent chat
```

## Task tracker

Claude keeps your task tracker up to date during a chat. You can also run these commands yourself.

```
daily-driver tracker add      # add a task ({% if "job_search" in plugins %}job, {% endif %}errand, milestone, or similar)
daily-driver tracker list     # list tracked tasks
daily-driver tracker update   # update status or notes on a task
daily-driver tracker stats    # counts by status and category
```

{% if "job_search" in plugins %}
## Job search

```
daily-driver jobs run              # search your job sites and save new jobs
daily-driver jobs discover-boards  # find company job pages (Greenhouse, Ashby, Lever) that list your roles
daily-driver jobs backfill         # fill in empty details for saved jobs
daily-driver jobs promote          # copy a saved job into your tracker
daily-driver jobs status           # show the last run and job counts by status
daily-driver jobs prune            # archive old jobs you are done with
daily-driver jobs verify           # close saved jobs that are no longer posted
```

{% endif %}
## Status and focus

```
daily-driver status           # totals, items with no update in 14 days, and recent activity
daily-driver focus on         # pause scheduled check-in reminders while you focus
daily-driver focus off        # turn check-in reminders back on
```

## Maintenance

```
daily-driver doctor           # check that your workspace works
daily-driver doctor --fix     # repair problems and keep your edits
daily-driver doctor --reset   # repair problems and replace Daily Driver files (your edits to them are lost)
```

## Configuration

Edit `.dd-config.yaml` in this directory to configure categories, {% if "job_search" in plugins %}job sources, {% endif %}daily schedule, and other workspace settings.

## Files Daily Driver supplies

Daily Driver supplies the files in `.claude/commands/daily-driver/`, `.claude/agents/daily-driver/`, and `.claude/hooks/`. After you upgrade, `daily-driver doctor` shows a WARNING named `Workspace drift`. Run `daily-driver doctor --fix` to update them:

- It keeps your edits to these files.
- It deletes `.md` files you added to `.claude/commands/daily-driver/` or `.claude/agents/daily-driver/`, and `.sh` files you added to `.claude/hooks/`. Put your own commands in `.claude/commands/user/`.
- It replaces the allow rules saved in `.claude/settings.local.json`.

`daily-driver doctor --reset` replaces all of these files with fresh copies. Your edits to them, and files you added to them, are lost.

This `README.md` is updated the same way. `doctor --fix` keeps your edits to it. `doctor --reset` overwrites it.

## Help

Run `daily-driver help` for lists of valid values, or `daily-driver COMMAND --help` for the options of one command. Full guides are in the `docs` folder of the [daily-driver repository](https://github.com/skoonin/daily-driver).
